+### Merging duplicates
+
+Staff can merge two distinct, non-closed tickets from the same customer. For example, `POST /api/v1/tickets/42/merge` with `{"merge":{"target_id":57}}` closes ticket 42 and sets its `merged_into_id` to 57. Both staff and portal lists and detail views include `merged_into_id` (`null` for unmerged tickets). `closed` is set only by merging, not by PATCH.
+
+Each ticket retains its comments and gets a private note identifying the other ticket. To override the text or visibility on either side, supply `source_comment` or `target_comment`:
+
+```json
+{"merge":{"target_id":57,"source_comment":{"body":"Continuing in ticket 57.","public":true},"target_comment":{"body":"Duplicate checked.","public":false}}}
+```
+
+Merge notes never send email. Closing the source is visible to its customer; on the target only a public note changes customer-visible activity. The target keeps its status, assignment and reply address. The closed source stays readable, but rejects edits and email replies (they are not forwarded). Normal unassignment on suspension, membership removal or group deletion still applies. If 57 later merges into 63, ticket 42 still links to 57.
+
